      <table class="feed-table" aria-label="NSE Financial Results live feed">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Company</th>
            <th>Period</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Audited?</th>
            <th>Period Ended</th>
            <th>Published</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="fr-body">
          {initialFR.length > 0 ? (
            initialFR.map(item => (
              <tr>
                <td class="company-name">{item.company}</td>
                <td><span class="results-badge badge-q">{item.period}</span></td>
                <td style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#9bacc8">{item.consolidated}</td>
                <td>
                  <span class={`results-badge ${item.audited.toLowerCase().includes('audited') ? 'badge-audited' : 'badge-unaudited'}`}>
                    {item.audited}
                  </span>
                </td>
                <td style="font-weight:600;color:#e8edf7;font-size:0.88rem;white-space:nowrap">{item.periodEnd}</td>
                <td style="color:#6b7a99;font-size:0.82rem;white-space:nowrap">{item.pubDate}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          ) : (
            <tr><td colspan="6"><div class="empty-state"><div class="icon">📭</div><p>No new results posted right now. <a href="https://www.nseindia.com/companies-listing/corporate-filings-financial-results" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on NSE →</a></p></div></td></tr>
          )}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Explainer -->
  <div class="prose-section">
    <h2>What Are NSE Board Meeting Notices?</h2>
    <p>
      All NSE-listed companies are required to notify the exchange at least <strong>2 business days</strong>
      before a board meeting where material decisions — including quarterly results, dividends, buybacks,
      or fund raises — will be discussed. This is your advance warning of upcoming catalysts for a stock.
    </p>
    <p>
      For investors, board meeting notices for <strong>financial results</strong> are especially important.
      They tell you exactly when a company will announce its Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4 numbers. If you hold that stock
      in your portfolio, you can plan accordingly. Use Arthavi's
      <a href="/portfolio-tracker-india">portfolio tracker</a> to monitor all your holdings
      and see their current performance before results day.
    </p>

    <h2>Understanding NSE Quarterly Financial Results</h2>
    <p>
      Indian companies report financial results on a quarterly basis: <strong>Q1 (Apr–Jun)</strong>,
      <strong>Q2 (Jul–Sep)</strong>, <strong>Q3 (Oct–Dec)</strong>, and <strong>Q4 / Annual (Jan–Mar)</strong>.
      The Q2 FY2026 results season (for July–September 2026) typically runs through October–November 2026.
    </p>
    <p>
      Results include revenue, EBITDA, PAT (Profit After Tax), EPS, and management guidance.
      They are disclosed as XBRL filings on NSE, and the key metrics are available within minutes of filing.
      <strong>Stock prices often move 5–20%</strong> on result day based on how the numbers compare to market expectations.
    </p>
    <p>
      If any of these companies are in your portfolio, track their impact on your XIRR and net worth live
      on <a href="/portfolio-tracker-india">Arthavi's portfolio dashboard</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="faq-section" aria-label="FAQ about NSE board meetings and results">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details class="faq-item" id="faq-bm">
      <summary>What is an NSE board meeting notice?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        An NSE board meeting notice is a mandatory disclosure filed by listed companies at least 2 business days before a board meeting. It states the date and agenda — most importantly whether dividend declaration, quarterly results, stock split, or fundraising is on the agenda.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" id="faq-q2">
      <summary>When do NSE Q2 FY2026 results come out?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        NSE Q2 FY2026 results (July–September 2026 quarter) are typically announced by companies between October and November 2026. Large-cap companies like TCS, Infosys, HCL, HDFC Bank, and Reliance typically go first, followed by mid and small caps. Board meetings for these results are announced 2 days in advance on this page.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" id="faq-impact">
      <summary>How do quarterly results affect my stock portfolio?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        Quarterly financial results reveal a company's revenue, profit, and margins for that period. Strong results (beating expectations) typically push stock prices up; weak results cause sell-offs. Knowing result dates helps you make informed decisions about your holdings. Arthavi's portfolio tracker shows your live XIRR and net worth so you can see real-time impact.
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" id="faq-xbrl">
      <summary>What is the XBRL format used in NSE financial results?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        XBRL (eXtensible Business Reporting Language) is the standardised format mandated by SEBI for filing financial results with NSE. It makes financial data machine-readable. NSE's RSS feed links to the XBRL XML files directly, which contain structured data on revenue, PAT, EPS, and more.
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <!-- Related pages -->
  <div style="margin-top:2.5rem;padding-top:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
    <p style="font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:#4b5f7a;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Related Pages</p>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.6rem;">
      <a href="/nse-corporate-actions-today/" style="background:var(--card-bg,#111827);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);color:#8daac4;padding:0.45rem 1rem;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.88rem;">NSE Corporate Actions Today</a>
      <a href="/portfolio-tracker-india/" style="background:var(--card-bg,#111827);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);color:#8daac4;padding:0.45rem 1rem;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.88rem;">Best Portfolio Tracker India</a>
      <a href="/stock-portfolio-tracker-india/" style="background:var(--card-bg,#111827);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);color:#8daac4;padding:0.45rem 1rem;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.88rem;">Stock Portfolio Tracker India</a>
      <a href="/portfolio-analytics-india/" style="background:var(--card-bg,#111827);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);color:#8daac4;padding:0.45rem 1rem;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-size:0.88rem;">Portfolio Analytics India</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</main>

<script is:inline>
(function () {
  const PROXIES = [
    url => 'https://api.allorigins.win/raw?url=' + encodeURIComponent(url),
    url => 'https://corsproxy.io/?' + encodeURIComponent(url)
  ];
  const BM_URL  = 'https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/content/RSS/Board_Meetings.xml';
  const FR_URL  = 'https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/content/RSS/Financial_Results.xml';

  function extract(desc, key) {
    const re = new RegExp(key + ':([^|\\n]+)', 'i');
    const m = desc.match(re);
    return m ? m[1].trim() : '—';
  }

  function periodBadge(period) {
    const p = (period || '').toUpperCase();
    if (p.includes('ANNUAL')) return '<span class="results-badge badge-annual">Annual</span>';
    if (p.includes('QUARTER') || p.includes('FOURTH') || p.includes('THIRD') || p.includes('SECOND') || p.includes('FIRST')) return '<span class="results-badge badge-q">Quarterly</span>';
    return `<span class="results-badge badge-q">${period || '—'}</span>`;
  }
  function auditedBadge(val) {
    return val && val.toLowerCase().includes('audited')
      ? '<span class="results-badge badge-audited">Audited</span>'
      : '<span class="results-badge badge-unaudited">Unaudited</span>';
  }

  async function fetchWithFallback(url) {
    for (const proxyFn of PROXIES) {
      try {
        const res = await fetch(proxyFn(url), { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(7000) });
        if (res.ok) {
          const text = await res.text();
          if (text && text.includes('<rss')) return text;
        }
      } catch (e) {
        // next proxy
      }
    }
    return null;
  }

  async function loadBM() {
    try {
      const text = await fetchWithFallback(BM_URL);
      if (!text) throw new Error('BM fetch failed');

      const xml = new DOMParser().parseFromString(text, 'application/xml');
      const lastBuild = xml.querySelector('lastBuildDate');
      if (lastBuild) {
        document.getElementById('bm-updated').textContent = lastBuild.textContent.trim();
      }

      const items = Array.from(xml.querySelectorAll('item'));
      if (items.length) {
        document.getElementById('bm-body').innerHTML = items.map(item => {
          const title = item.querySelector('title')?.textContent?.trim() || '';
          const desc = item.querySelector('description')?.textContent?.trim() || '';
          const pub = item.querySelector('pubDate')?.textContent?.trim() || '—';
          const company = title.split('\n')[0].trim();
          const meetDate = extract(desc, 'BOARD MEETING DATE') !== '—' ? extract(desc, 'BOARD MEETING DATE') : extract(desc, 'DATE');
          return `<tr>
            <td class="company-name">${company}</td>
            <td style="font-weight:600;color:#e8edf7;white-space:nowrap">${meetDate}</td>
            <td style="font-size:0.85rem;color:#9bacc8;max-width:320px">${desc.substring(0, 120)}…</td>
            <td style="color:#6b7a99;font-size:0.85rem;white-space:nowrap">${pub}</td>
          </tr>`;
        }).join('');
      }
    } catch (e) {
      console.warn('BM feed update skipped:', e);
    }
  }

  async function loadFR() {
    try {
      const text = await fetchWithFallback(FR_URL);
      if (!text) throw new Error('FR fetch failed');

      const xml = new DOMParser().parseFromString(text, 'application/xml');
      const lastBuild = xml.querySelector('lastBuildDate');
      if (lastBuild) {
        document.getElementById('fr-updated').textContent = lastBuild.textContent.trim();
      }

      const items = Array.from(xml.querySelectorAll('item'));
      if (items.length) {
        document.getElementById('fr-body').innerHTML = items.map(item => {
          const title = item.querySelector('title')?.textContent?.trim() || '';
          const desc = item.querySelector('description')?.textContent?.trim() || '';
          const pub = item.querySelector('pubDate')?.textContent?.trim() || '—';
          const company = title.split('\n')[0].trim();
          const period = extract(desc, 'PERIOD');
          const relating = extract(desc, 'RELATING TO');
          const audited = extract(desc, 'AUDITED/UNAUDITED');
          const periodEnd = extract(desc, 'PERIOD ENDED');
          const consolidated = extract(desc, 'CONSOLIDATED/NON-CONSOLIDATED');
          return `<tr>
            <td class="company-name">${company}</td>
            <td>${periodBadge(relating)}</td>
            <td style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#9bacc8">${consolidated !== '—' ? consolidated : '—'}</td>
            <td>${auditedBadge(audited)}</td>
            <td style="font-weight:600;color:#e8edf7;font-size:0.88rem;white-space:nowrap">${periodEnd}</td>
            <td style="color:#6b7a99;font-size:0.82rem;white-space:nowrap">${pub}</td>
          </tr>`;
        }).join('');
      }
    } catch (e) {
      console.warn('FR feed update skipped:', e);
    }
  }

  // Tab switching
  document.getElementById('tab-bm').addEventListener('click', () => {
    document.getElementById('tab-bm').classList.add('active');
    document.getElementById('tab-fr').classList.remove('active');
    document.getElementById('panel-bm').classList.add('active');
    document.getElementById('panel-fr').classList.remove('active');
  });
  document.getElementById('tab-fr').addEventListener('click', () => {
    document.getElementById('tab-fr').classList.add('active');
    document.getElementById('tab-bm').classList.remove('active');
    document.getElementById('panel-fr').classList.add('active');
    document.getElementById('panel-bm').classList.remove('active');
    if (!document.getElementById('fr-body').innerHTML.includes('<tr>')) loadFR();
  });

  // Auto-refresh every 5 min
  loadBM();
  loadFR();
  setInterval(() => { loadBM(); loadFR(); }, 5 * 60 * 1000);
})();
</script>

</Layout>
